<div class="nexa-faq-page" data-section-id="{{ section.id }}">
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <div class="faq-hero">
    <nav class="faq-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span class="sep">/</span>
      <span class="current">Laptop Compatibility & Hardware FAQ</span>
    </nav>
    <div class="faq-badge-pill">
      <span>💡 ZERO-GUESSWORK HARDWARE GUIDE</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="faq-title">Laptop Compatibility & Setup FAQ</h1>
    <p class="faq-subtitle">
      Clear, straightforward answers about USB-C Power Delivery, multi-monitor display limits, MacBook dual-screen configurations, and plug types. Everything you need to get your desk right the first time.
    </p>

    <!-- Quick Category Tabs -->
    <div class="faq-category-pills">
      <button type="button" class="faq-cat-btn active" onclick="filterFaqCategory('all', this)">⚡ All Questions</button>
      <button type="button" class="faq-cat-btn" onclick="filterFaqCategory('laptop-fit', this)">💻 Laptop Fit & USB-C</button>
      <button type="button" class="faq-cat-btn" onclick="filterFaqCategory('screens', this)">🖥️ Dual Monitors & Displays</button>
      <button type="button" class="faq-cat-btn" onclick="filterFaqCategory('charging', this)">🔋 Charging & Wattage</button>
      <button type="button" class="faq-cat-btn" onclick="filterFaqCategory('delivery', this)">📦 UK Delivery & 30-Day Trial</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="faq-content-grid">
    <!-- Main Accordion List -->
    <div class="faq-accordion-container">

      <!-- Category: Laptop Fit & USB-C -->
      <div class="faq-item" data-category="laptop-fit">
        <button type="button" class="faq-question-btn" onclick="toggleFaq(this)" aria-expanded="true">
          <span class="faq-q-text">
            <span class="faq-q-badge badge-fit">Laptop Fit</span>
            Will a Nexa docking station work with my Windows or MacBook laptop?
          </span>
          <span class="faq-chevron-icon">
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
          </span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer-panel" style="max-height: 500px;">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            <p><strong>Yes!</strong> All Nexa docking stations (D1, D2, D3) utilize industry-standard USB-C and Thunderbolt protocols that are natively supported on:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Apple MacBooks:</strong> M1, M2, M3, M4 (Air and Pro) and Intel MacBooks running macOS Monterey or newer.</li>
              <li><strong>Windows Laptops:</strong> Dell XPS/Latitude, Lenovo ThinkPad/Yoga, HP Spectre/EliteBook, Microsoft Surface, Asus, and Acer with USB-C or Thunderbolt 3/4.</li>
              <li><strong>Legacy USB-A PCs:</strong> Compatible with our <strong>D4 Connect A</strong> USB hub.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>You do not need to install any custom drivers; your laptop configures all ports automatically within 3 seconds of plugging in.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item" data-category="laptop-fit">
        <button type="button" class="faq-question-btn" onclick="toggleFaq(this)" aria-expanded="false">
          <span class="faq-q-text">
            <span class="faq-q-badge badge-fit">USB-C Check</span>
            How do I tell if my laptop's USB-C port supports video output and charging?
          </span>
          <span class="faq-chevron-icon">
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
          </span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer-panel">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            <p>Look at the small icon next to your laptop's USB-C port:</p>
            <div class="port-explanation-cards">
              <div class="port-card">
                <span class="port-icon">⚡</span>
                <strong>Lightning Bolt:</strong> Thunderbolt 3/4 or USB4. Transmits dual 4K video, ultra-fast 40Gbps data, and full laptop charging.
              </div>
              <div class="port-card">
                <span class="port-icon">Ⓓ</span>
                <strong>DisplayPort (D):</strong> Supports DisplayPort Alternate Mode (video out) and USB-PD charging.
              </div>
              <div class="port-card">
                <span class="port-icon">🔋</span>
                <strong>Battery Plug:</strong> Supports Power Delivery charging.
              </div>
            </div>
            <p style="margin-top: 1rem;">Not sure? Simply run our <a href="/pages/find-my-setup" style="color: #38bdf8; font-weight: 600;">Find My Setup Quiz</a> and we will verify your laptop automatically.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Category: Displays & Dual Screens -->
      <div class="faq-item" data-category="screens">
        <button type="button" class="faq-question-btn" onclick="toggleFaq(this)" aria-expanded="false">
          <span class="faq-q-text">
            <span class="faq-q-badge badge-screen">Dual Monitors</span>
            Can I connect two independent extended screens to an Apple Mac?
          </span>
          <span class="faq-chevron-icon">
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
          </span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer-panel">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            <p>Here is the honest breakdown of Apple's display architecture:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Base M1 / M2 / M3 MacBook Air & 13" Pro:</strong> Apple's base chips natively support <strong>1 external display</strong> through a single dock cable (plus the laptop screen). The <strong>D1 Link 65</strong> provides full 4K@60Hz for this setup.</li>
              <li><strong>MacBook Pro with M-Pro / M-Max Chips:</strong> Natively support <strong>dual and triple extended external displays</strong> at full 4K 60Hz. The <strong>D2 Link 100</strong> and <strong>D3 Pro 100</strong> docks power dual displays effortlessly.</li>
              <li><strong>Windows Laptops:</strong> Standard Windows machines support MST (Multi-Stream Transport), allowing the <strong>D2 Link 100</strong> to run dual distinct extended desktop screens over a single USB-C cable.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item" data-category="screens">
        <button type="button" class="faq-question-btn" onclick="toggleFaq(this)" aria-expanded="false">
          <span class="faq-q-text">
            <span class="faq-q-badge badge-screen">Resolution</span>
            What refresh rates and screen resolutions do Nexa monitors support?
          </span>
          <span class="faq-chevron-icon">
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
          </span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer-panel">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            <p>All Nexa monitors (M1, M2, M3, M4) feature high-grade IPS panels with anti-glare coatings:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>M1 27" HDMI Monitor (£145):</strong> 1080p Full HD / 75Hz with ultra-sharp text clarity and eye-saver blue light reduction.</li>
              <li><strong>M2 27" DisplayPort Monitor (£189):</strong> 1440p QHD / 100Hz fluid high-refresh display ideal for coding, data sheets, and multi-window work.</li>
              <li><strong>M3 27" USB-C Monitor (£250):</strong> 4K Ultra HD IPS panel with direct USB-C single-cable video + 65W charging pass-through.</li>
              <li><strong>M4 15.6" Portable Monitor (£199):</strong> 1080p FHD USB-C lightweight travel display powered directly by your laptop.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Category: Charging & Power Delivery -->
      <div class="faq-item" data-category="charging">
        <button type="button" class="faq-question-btn" onclick="toggleFaq(this)" aria-expanded="false">
          <span class="faq-q-text">
            <span class="faq-q-badge badge-power">Power & Wattage</span>
            Do I need 65W or 100W USB-C Power Delivery charging?
          </span>
          <span class="faq-chevron-icon">
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
          </span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer-panel">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            <p>It depends on your laptop model and power requirements:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Choose 65W (D1 Link 65):</strong> Ideal for ultrabooks, 13"–14" laptops, MacBook Air, Dell XPS 13, HP Envy, and business laptops that use 45W–65W chargers.</li>
              <li><strong>Choose 100W (D2 Link 100 or D3 Pro 100):</strong> Recommended for 15"–16" MacBook Pros, mobile workstation laptops, CAD computers, and gaming rigs that draw up to 90W–100W under heavy workloads.</li>
            </ul>
            <p><em>Safety note:</em> All Nexa docks feature intelligent GaN PD negotiation — a 100W dock safely and automatically steps down to deliver 45W or 65W to smaller laptops without overheating.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item" data-category="charging">
        <button type="button" class="faq-question-btn" onclick="toggleFaq(this)" aria-expanded="false">
          <span class="faq-q-text">
            <span class="faq-q-badge badge-power">Cables</span>
            Are high-speed video cables and UK power bricks included in the box?
          </span>
          <span class="faq-chevron-icon">
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
          </span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer-panel">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            <p><strong>Yes, 100% complete in the box.</strong> We believe you shouldn't have to buy extra cables on Amazon just to set up your desk:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Docks:</strong> Include the dedicated UK power brick + 1.0m braided high-speed 100W host USB-C cable.</li>
              <li><strong>Monitors:</strong> Include HDMI/DP video cables + UK 3-pin power lead.</li>
              <li><strong>Bundle kits:</strong> Include all necessary interconnect cables and velcro cable management ties.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Category: Delivery & Guarantee -->
      <div class="faq-item" data-category="delivery">
        <button type="button" class="faq-question-btn" onclick="toggleFaq(this)" aria-expanded="false">
          <span class="faq-q-text">
            <span class="faq-q-badge badge-trust">UK Delivery</span>
            What are your UK shipping times and return policies?
          </span>
          <span class="faq-chevron-icon">
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
          </span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer-panel">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            <p>We dispatch all orders from our UK logistics hub:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Free Fast UK Delivery:</strong> Free on all complete desk setups and orders over £300 (Royal Mail Tracked 24 / DPD).</li>
              <li><strong>Standard Delivery:</strong> £7.95 for orders under £300, delivered in 1–2 working days.</li>
              <li><strong>30-Day Risk-Free Home Trial:</strong> Set it up on your desk and try it for 30 days. If it doesn't fit your workspace or workflow, return it for a 100% refund with free return labels.</li>
              <li><strong>2-Year Nexa UK Hardware Warranty:</strong> Full replacement guarantee against any hardware faults.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- Quick Sidebar Widget -->
    <aside class="faq-sidebar">
      <div class="faq-card-support">
        <div class="card-icon">⚡</div>
        <h3 class="card-title">Still Not Sure About Your Laptop?</h3>
        <p class="card-desc">
          Take our interactive 30-second setup finder quiz. We check your laptop specs and build the guaranteed compatible bundle.
        </p>
        <a href="/pages/find-my-setup" class="btn-quiz-cta">
          <span>Launch Setup Finder Quiz</span>
          <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-card-support card-secondary">
        <div class="card-icon">⚖️</div>
        <h3 class="card-title">Compare Dock Specs</h3>
        <p class="card-desc">
          View side-by-side ports, wattage, resolution limits, and prices for D1, D2, D3, and D4.
        </p>
        <a href="/pages/compare-docks" class="btn-compare-cta">
          <span>Compare Docks Side-by-Side &rarr;</span>
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-card-support card-contact">
        <div class="card-icon">💬</div>
        <h3 class="card-title">Need UK Human Advice?</h3>
        <p class="card-desc">
          Have an unusual corporate laptop or dual-monitor setup? Speak directly to our UK desk specialists.
        </p>
        <a href="/pages/contact" class="btn-contact-cta">
          <span>Contact UK Support</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</div>

